# Build context allowlist for apps/api/Dockerfile.
#
# Everything is excluded first, then only the files the image needs are added
# back. A denylist would eventually leak something: this repository holds a
# private SDK submodule, a local corpus, notebooks, browser captures, and local
# environment files, and any of them could otherwise reach an image layer by
# being added later.
**

# The API's dependency metadata. README.md is declared by pyproject.toml, so
# the wheel build needs it.
!apps/api/pyproject.toml
!apps/api/uv.lock
!apps/api/README.md

# The served API itself. `modelling` is not here on purpose: it is offline
# evaluation support and is excluded from the production wheel.
!apps/api/server/**
!apps/api/server/**/

# The sanitised benchmark evidence the read-only model-summary route serves.
# Both files are already public in the repository, aggregate-only, and the
# route still validates the report's status, feature list, and dataset
# checksum before serving anything.
!docs/contracts/model-training-contract.v1.json
!docs/proposals/fast-path-model-release.candidate.json

# Never, under any pattern above.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
